  "description": "Six-channel 4-20 mA indicator and data acquisition module with two alarm relays, six LEDs and totalisers (special version), with Modbus RTU",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "Presys, DMY-2015-mA / TY-2095 special version sheet EE1018-00 (19 February 2005)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Indicador digital multi-ponto DMY-2015-mA, modulo de aquisicao de dados TY-2095, versao especial",
      "version": "EE1018-00",
      "date": "2005-02-19",
      "url": "https://presys.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/multiponto-aquisitor-009-02-05-ee-1018-00.pdf",
      "note": "register and coil tables, linked in issue #391"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Special version with six isolated 4-20 mA inputs. The sheet says its information takes priority over the instrument's technical manual.",
    "The document numbers registers and coils from 00 and does not say whether they are the addresses sent on the wire; they are taken as wire addresses (address_base 0). If a read is off by one, try address_base 1.",
    "The document does not give the serial settings. The slave address (0 to 99), baud rate (300 to 9600 bps) and parity are registers; 9600 bps, no parity and slave 1 are placeholders.",
    "Values shown with a decimal point on the display are sent without it. Process variables, setpoints and hysteresis values depend on the decimals of their channel and are given raw. The digital filter constant (one decimal) is scaled; percent values are given raw.",
    "The document does not say which Modbus function reads the registers; they are taken as holding registers. Registers and coils not listed (for example 18 to 23, 37 to 42, 49 to 54) are not mapped. The sheet's example mentions register 55 for the filter, but the filter registers are 67 to 72 in the table.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "N",
  "databits": 8,
  "stopbits": 1,
  "address_base": 0,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "x_status": "official",
